# Security First

## Objective

Security is not optional. Every change must preserve confidentiality, integrity, and safe failure modes.

## Requirements

- Validate and sanitize all untrusted input (HTTP, files, user config, IPC, CLI args).
- Never commit secrets; use env/config mechanisms the project already uses.
- Parameterized queries / prepared statements for SQL  -  never string-concat SQL.
- Least privilege for credentials, tokens, and file paths.
- Do not expose stack traces, internal paths, or SQL in user-facing errors.
> **If this project has no HTTP/REST API surface:** apply the same principles to the nearest public interface (module APIs, SDK callbacks, CLI commands, RPC, message contracts) or skip.

## Review Triggers

Auth changes, new endpoints, file I/O, crypto, dependency bumps, deserialization.

